WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.255
Lesson 12.1.

00:00:02.255 --> 00:00:03.620
Your balance sheet.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.683
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:05.683 --> 00:00:07.927
be able to build a personal on-chain

00:00:07.927 --> 00:00:10.414
balance sheet and read the three numbers

00:00:10.414 --> 00:00:13.205
that matter: equity, LTV and liquidity runway.

00:00:14.505 --> 00:00:15.795
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.795 --> 00:00:17.480
First, the key ideas.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.195
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:20.195 --> 00:00:21.720
Then, your checklist.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.882
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:25.182 --> 00:00:28.385
Banks fail from liquidity (can't pay today) more often

00:00:28.385 --> 00:00:31.247
than from solvency (owe more than they own).

00:00:31.247 --> 00:00:32.407
Track both.

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.913
First, Assets: everything you own, at

00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:38.642
market value: collateral, yield positions, reserves.

00:00:38.642 --> 00:00:43.482
Next, Liabilities: everything you owe: loans, margin, any payables.

00:00:43.482 --> 00:00:46.817
Then, Equity = assets − liabilities.

00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:48.822
This is what's actually yours.

00:00:48.822 --> 00:00:52.937
Also, LTV = debt ÷ collateral.

00:00:52.937 --> 00:00:54.502
Your bank's leverage.

00:00:54.502 --> 00:00:58.268
And finally, Liquidity runway = liquid reserve

00:00:58.268 --> 00:01:01.793
÷ monthly obligations (spending + interest).

00:01:03.093 --> 00:01:05.608
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:05.608 --> 00:01:12.202
$300,000 collateral, $60,000 debt at 5%, $40,000 stablecoin

00:01:12.202 --> 00:01:18.357
reserve, $5,000 a month spending: the calculator Equity

00:01:18.357 --> 00:01:23.713
$280,000 times L.T.V. 20% , health factor 4.0.

00:01:23.713 --> 00:01:28.253
Obligations $5,250 a month ($250 of it

00:01:28.253 --> 00:01:33.093
interest) to reserve covers 7.6 months.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.549
Policy checks: L.T.V. at most 30% ✓

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:37.527
, health factor at least 2 ✓

00:01:37.527 --> 00:01:39.573
, reserve at least 6 months ✓.

00:01:40.873 --> 00:01:42.333
Here's your checklist.

00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:43.868
Do it now, for real.

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:46.233
First, Balance sheet updated weekly.

00:01:46.233 --> 00:01:50.078
Next, Equity, LTV and runway tracked over time.

00:01:50.078 --> 00:01:53.309
And finally, Policy limits written (max

00:01:53.309 --> 00:01:55.328
LTV, min HF, min runway).

00:01:56.628 --> 00:01:57.838
Question 1.

00:01:57.838 --> 00:02:01.453
Assets $500k, debt $100k.

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:02.078
Equity?

00:02:06.498 --> 00:02:08.573
The answer: $400k.

00:02:09.873 --> 00:02:11.118
Question 2.

00:02:11.118 --> 00:02:15.003
Reserve $30k, obligations $6k/month.

00:02:15.003 --> 00:02:15.668
Runway?

00:02:20.088 --> 00:02:23.203
The answer: 5 months, below a 6-month policy.

00:02:24.503 --> 00:02:25.773
Question 3.

00:02:25.773 --> 00:02:28.198
Why track liquidity separately from equity?

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:35.022
The answer: You can be solvent and still

00:02:35.022 --> 00:02:37.132
be forced to sell at the worst time

00:02:37.132 --> 00:02:39.243
if you can't meet obligations today.

00:02:40.543 --> 00:02:41.788
Let's recap.

00:02:41.788 --> 00:02:44.723
Assets: everything you own, at market value.

00:02:44.723 --> 00:02:46.998
Liabilities: everything you owe.

00:02:46.998 --> 00:02:49.326
Equity = assets − liabilities:

00:02:49.326 --> 00:02:51.878
This is what's actually yours.

00:02:51.878 --> 00:02:56.407
LTV = debt ÷ collateral: Your bank's leverage.

00:02:57.707 --> 00:03:00.222
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:00.222 --> 00:03:03.522
Next up, Lesson 12.2: Custody architecture:

00:03:03.522 --> 00:03:06.372
vault, multisig and spending policies.
